    "long_instructions": "# Scenario\r\n\r\n#### During a 9th grade science unit on ecosystems, students were given time in class to explore how energy moves through an ecosystem. They had already completed readings, taken notes on key vocabulary (producers, consumers, trophic levels), and participated in a short food web simulation earlier in the week.\r\n\r\n#### During independent work time, students were allowed to use an AI tool as one of several available resources.\r\n\r\n#### After class, students were asked to complete a quick exit reflection:\r\n\r\n#### *How helpful was the AI tool in improving your understanding today? Explain briefly.*\r\n\r\n#### The responses were mixed.  \r\n* #### Some students wrote that the explanation “made it click.”  \r\n* #### Others said the response was “too long” or “basically what was already in the textbook.”  \r\n* #### A few said it was helpful at first but “kind of confusing after a while.”\r\n\r\n#### After class, you review the anonymous prompt logs from that period. Below are three prompts students submitted:\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"width:80%; margin:0 auto 18px auto;\">\r\n  <div style=\"background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px;\">\r\n    <div style=\"font-size:16px;\">\r\n      ✨ Explain ecosystems.\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"width:80%; margin:0 auto 18px auto;\">\r\n  <div style=\"background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px;\">\r\n    <div style=\"font-size:16px;\">\r\n      ✨ Explain ecosystems in detail.\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"width:80%; margin:0 auto 18px auto;\">\r\n  <div style=\"background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px;\">\r\n    <div style=\"font-size:16px;\">\r\n      ✨ I’m a 9th grade student learning about ecosystems for the first time. Explain how energy moves through an ecosystem using clear language and one specific example. Keep it under 200 words.\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Reflection\r\n\r\n> #### In the reflection box below, answer the following questions:\r\n> #### &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp 1. What differences would you expect in the responses generated from these three prompts? Why?\r\n> #### &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp 2. What sort of guidance or structure might you provide to the students to help them write more effective prompts?",
